    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn algebraic identities and factorisation shortcuts.\n\nThis lesson uses the methods and question patterns from the Simplification chapter.\n\nWe will keep each step small: understand one rule, see it with numbers, then try a similar question.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The square identities turn a long multiplication into a short calculation.\n\n(a+b)^2 = a^2+b^2+2ab\n(a-b)^2 = a^2+b^2-2ab.\n\nUse them when you know a+b, a-b, or when an expanded expression already has the pattern.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
